{"name":"Velvet Touch","hex":"#523544","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"},{"term":"touch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Primarily physical senses.\n To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.","The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"},{"title":"Somatosensory system","blocks":[{"text":"The somatosensory system, or somatic sensory system, is a subset of the sensory nervous system. The main functions of the somatosensory system are the perception of external stimuli, the perception of internal stimuli, 